  "interpretation": "Webhook delivery contract holds: HMAC-SHA256 signatures over <timestamp>.<body> verify against the declared secret and refuse wrong-secret, tampered, and replayed-stale deliveries; every terminal transition fires exactly once across jobs, evals, fine-tuning jobs, and both batch surfaces \u2014 repeated cancels and repeated GETs never re-fire; 5xx retries bound at three attempts with capped backoff, 4xx is definitive, dead and stalling endpoints give up loudly into a recorded 'failed' verdict; the delivered body is the final record shape (finished_at populated, terminal status consistent with GET); callback verdicts surface on every record's GET; callback_secret never serializes to GETs, deliveries, or the journal; scheme/userinfo smuggling and secret-without-URL all refuse 422 at create; and an unresolvable host never hangs the request path.",
